- title: Build row-fused statistics and activation
- difficulty_1_to_5: 3
- description: Implement one independent program per logical row that computes FP32 row moments, derives the Gaussian cutoff, then rereads the row and emits BF16 ReLU outputs.
- rationale: This minimizes launches and temporary traffic while matching the natural independence of rows. Reloading input avoids keeping a full 4096-16384 element row live across the reduction.

